Z||000000||VelociFero||11-29-2000||06:01 PM||||Hey there, nice forum!<P><BR>I have a totally stock 86 GT in great shape that I'd like to start driving again.  My question is where do I go from here?  I replaced the V6 a few years ago, because it threw a rod and burned at only 45,000 miles.  That's actually why I gave it to my sister -- just too angry to drive it anymore.  However, with her going to college and getting a new car, I'll take it back as another "toy" and want to do some upgrades.<P>Here are a few ?s:<BR>1.  I am aware of some recalls; how do I find out if they have been done to my car?  Also, since the whole engine was replaced, would the recessary changes have already been made?<BR>2.  Lowering springs and new shocks...  What would be a decent set to use for maybe 1" to 1.5" drop with a good balance between ride and cornering.<BR>3.  Speed!  What can be don to deliver more of this?  Keep in mind I'd rather lose any of my low-end torque... in fact, I'd love to have plenty more.  <BR>4.  What else can you tell me about my car?  I never got into it as much as I have with my MR2s, so I've learned very little about the Fiero.<P>Thanks, guys.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-29-2000||07:39 PM||||Recall: see if the rubber strip has been removed from the rear of the deck lid. Gone recall has been completed.<P>Lowering do a search on the forum on lowering Fieros.  Shocks can be Koni or any other type.  86's are easy to replace.<P>Speed: get a 3.4 engine, 3.8 engine, 3.8 s/c engine.  If you have deep pockets talk to V8 Archie for a v8 install.  Top speed for a stock 2.8 is maybe 120.  Don't know where in Illinois you can legally drive 120mph.<P>Want help for the Fiero: Twin Lakes Fiero in Paxton Illinois.  217 379 9140.  He is close by and does good work on Fiero fixes.||||reg||3
Z||000002||VelociFero||11-29-2000||08:58 PM||||Excellent.  Thank you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1991 2.2L MR2<BR>1986 GT Fiero <BR>00 Mustang (Black)<BR>00 Mustang (Silver)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mr2pages.com/members/velocifero/SmallMR2one.jpg"> ||||reg||14
